   690→\subsubsection*{Theme 5 -- Compaction Workflow}
   691→
   692→Twenty-four respondents (48\%) engaged with the \texttt{/compaction} command. Sixteen (67\% of this group) said the per-turn growth projection helped them identify the \emph{compaction point} --- the turn at which context would exceed the rot threshold --- before it happened. Eight participants requested an \emph{automatic compaction suggestion}: a chat message from \texttt{@tokalator} that fires when per-turn growth exceeds a user-configured threshold, analogous to VS Code v1.110's automatic compaction for Copilot sessions. Four participants noted that the \texttt{/compaction} output did not distinguish between tokens from files vs.\ tokens from conversation history, making it harder to decide whether to close tabs or summarize the conversation; this decomposition is a planned enhancement.
