\hl{These figures demonstrate that AI-assisted development at the individual practitioner level is economically accessible: a commercially publishable, 20,814-LOC multi-component toolkit was constructed in 30 calendar days for a total net AI compute cost of \$28.36. Context-aware tooling --- the very capability Tokalator provides --- directly enables this cost efficiency: by monitoring token budgets and closing low-relevance tabs before sending requests, developers reduce both the token count per request and the number of requests needed to achieve a correct result. The 49.8\% effective discount observed here reflects GitHub's account-level billing credits rather than in-session optimisation;} instrumented studies comparing token-budget-aware vs.\ unaware workflows remain a priority for future work (Section~\ref{sec:future}).

\subsection{Broader Impact}

