\subsection{Broader Impact}

\textit{(i) Cost optimization without the math.} The web platform turns economic theory into interactive tools that any developer can use, no LLM economics background required. Break-even analysis, Cobb--Douglas optimization, and conversation cost projection are each reduced to a form and a chart.

\textit{(ii) Educational resources.} The 10-lesson context engineering course at \url{https://tokalator.wiki/learn} progresses from token basics to production compaction patterns. The automated wiki aggregates articles from arXiv, OpenAI Cookbook, Anthropic, and Google AI docs on a bi-monthly schedule. The dictionary defines 41 terms across seven categories, contributing to vocabulary standardization in a field where terminology is still inconsistent~\cite{burnham2025context}.

\textit{(iii) Ecosystem contribution.} The catalog provides a structured starting point for teams adopting context engineering practices: reusable artifacts are auto-discovered from \texttt{copilot-contribution/} and \texttt{user-content/} using file-extension conventions, and the collection grows with community submissions. The MCP server enables any Claude Code user to access real BPE token counts without an API key or network call. Tokalator's context management best practices are also published as a reusable agent skill on skills.sh, installable via \texttt{npx skills add vfaraji89/tokalator} (\url{https://skills.sh}), making the token budget workflow available to any agent that supports the Agent Skills specification.

\textit{(iv) Marketplace adoption.} The VS~Code extension was published on the Visual Studio Code Marketplace on February~4, 2026. v3.1.2, released March~7, 2026, resolves the three bugs reported during community sessions and adds automatic Copilot model synchronization. Within its first 30 days (February~4 – March~8, 2026), it recorded 163~total acquisitions (installs and downloads combined) from 210~page views,
yielding a 77.62\% page-to-acquisition conversion rate (no published benchmark for the Marketplace average was available at time of writing). Of the 163 acquisitions, 19 are organic direct installs initiated from within VS~Code or via the Marketplace install button --- developers who discovered the extension independently, without referral links or community promotion. Figure~\ref{fig:marketplace} shows the daily acquisition trend and conversion funnel: activity peaked around February~8--14, coinciding with the most intensive development period (46~commits on February~8) when the extension was promoted across internal and community channels. The sustained long-tail acquisitions through late February and early March reflect ongoing organic discovery via the Marketplace search. Combined with the 220+ developers reached through community sessions, these figures indicate genuine practitioner demand for context budget tooling.

