1191:The survey comprised 10 items administered in person during the three community sessions (iLab/Kariyer.net, TechCareer, SaaS Bridge) and in a follow-up online session for remote participants, after each participant had used the Tokalator extension for at least one full working day. Responses were collected in real time by the first author through structured note-taking during the sessions and subsequently consolidated into a shared Excel file. Items~1--5 address the five core features (preview, tokenizer, model sync, session management, and compaction); Items~6--10 cover overall usability, recommendation intent, ease of installation, dashboard clarity, and enterprise feature interest. All items used a five-point Likert scale (1 = Strongly~Disagree / Not~Useful; 5 = Strongly~Agree / Very~Useful). Each rated item was followed by an optional open-text explanation, whose responses were inductively coded into the five themes reported in Section~\ref{sec:survey}.

