\end{table*}

\textit{Model attribution note.} The GitHub Copilot billing API does not expose per-request model attribution in the exported CSV. Based on developer session logs and the \texttt{request.model} field observed in Copilot extension events, the 1,413 premium requests are attributable to three preferred model backends: Claude Opus~4.6 (primary, Anthropic BPE), GPT~5.3 (OpenAI, \texttt{o200k\_base}), and GPT Codex~5.4 (OpenAI code-specialized, \texttt{o200k\_base}). The intensive-sprint sessions (February~6--11) predominantly used Claude Opus~4.6 for architectural and implementation tasks; GPT~5.3 and GPT Codex~5.4 were used for code completion, test generation, and documentation drafting in later sessions.

